`twisted.conch.ssh.keys.Key.verify` now takes an optional `acceptableAlgorithms` argument (a set of algorithm names) and raises `BadSignatureAlgorithmError` if the algorithm embedded in the signature is not one of them; the exception records both the algorithm that was used and the acceptable set. `twisted.conch.checkers` now passes the algorithm name from `MSG_USERAUTH_REQUEST` when verifying public key signatures, so a signature made under one algorithm can no longer be presented as if it had been made using a different one.
